schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Flat vs Hierarchical Organizational Structure
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    A contrast between pyramid-shaped organizations (departments, managers,
    executives, decisions flowing top-down) and flat, peer-coordinated
    structures where contributors take on roles by interest and capability
    rather than job title.
  source_traditions:
    - 20th-century theory of the firm (organizational hierarchy as a response
      to coordination-cost problems)
    - cooperative and associational governance (East African cooperatives cited
      in the article as a comparison point)
    - DAO/blockchain-native peer coordination
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Used in this article as the structural half of the DAO-vs-traditional-firm
    comparison, paired with the decision-making and capital-formation
    dimensions, and connected to the observation that traditional companies are
    geographically limited while DAOs are not.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - flatness as an absence of formal titles (this article's framing)
    - flatness as an absence of any power differential (a stronger, contested
      claim the article does not make)
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      flat-structure-vs-actual-power-distribution — the article itself
      cautions elsewhere (token concentration) that a flat org chart does not
      guarantee flat power; formal hierarchy and informal concentration are
      different things.
    - >-
      even-democratic-traditional-orgs-can-drift — the article notes that
      "even organizations founded on democratic principles can drift toward
      concentrated control over time," applying this critique to cooperatives,
      not only corporations.
  tensions:
    - >-
      flexibility-and-self-direction (flat) vs need-for-self-direction-without-
      management-support — flatness "creates flexibility but also requires
      self-direction," per the article.
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    Assuming "flat" automatically means "equal" erases the article's own later
    caution about token concentration recreating centralized control inside a
    nominally flat structure.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/daos-vs-traditional.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  work_order: wo-15f037f070f8
